@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# ECON-02B2d8 — Multi-source NPC construction logistics and allocations
+
+**Date:** November 1, 2026
+**Project:** Single Galaxy (original colony space game)
+**Baseline:** `SingleGalaxy_ECON02B2d7_NPC_Material_Logistics_Source_Tests_2026-11-01.zip`.
+**Development:** Local Linux; GitHub remains a repository, not the development hub. No repository upload in this milestone.
+
+## Completed scope
+
+ECON-02B2d8 extends previously authoritative colony construction supply custody into multiple **actually constructed and placed storage bins** in the same colony outpost. Crew scheduling, factory hardware, structures and inventory remain part of **one persistent `PersistentWorld`**, not a competing world writer.
+
+- Construction resources are tracked separately as unallocated local depot stock, available physical per-node stock, per-plan node reservations, named NPC carried cargo, delivered site-cell stock, and incorporated finished structures. Each transfer uses a `Simulation` Action with a persistent command/resource ledger receipt. A reservation removes physical stock from the free-node balance; it is not a virtual duplication. Each plan's allocation has a specific `node` and quantity.
+- Worker scheduler selects a reachable supply source deterministically using Manhattan transit score, choosing the lowest node ID as a tie-break. Physical walls and closed doors are respected by the grid route validator. This is deliberately local construction-grid navigation, **not** a 3D planetary/navmesh or inter-colony hauling system.
+- Real installed storage bins constrain construction-module occupancy: each existing storage node has 4 m³ nominal bin capacity and each construction module occupies 2 m³, so it can hold two modules at most. Existing stack and automated storage-link transfers also account for this occupied volume.
+- Two competing plans cannot reserve the same units twice. Reservations and node stock survive SQLite restart; cancellation releases unpicked reservations at the source. Already delivered materials are not silently refunded. A host-controlled `RecoverConstructionDelivery` action salvages unspent delivered modules into an actual named NPC's carrying inventory, after which they must be returned via a transfer.
+- Added `sg_construction_restock` assignments for existing, eligible colony residents. Supply jobs walk from the depot to the selected installed node, carry a bounded real cargo load, deposit modules, and persist location and task phase through shutdown/restart. Crew assignment checks prevent a resident from being assigned to construction and restocking concurrently. Cancellation while carrying schedules a physical return trip to the depot.
+- Added token/site-validated native `CREW_RESTOCK` / `CREW_RESTOCK_CANCEL` commands and relay endpoints `/factory/api/crew_restock` and `/factory/api/crew_restock_cancel`. `CREW_LIST` now reports aggregate depot/node/reserved/carried/delivered balances, up to 32 visible installed source nodes and active/historical restocking jobs. **The 32-row display limit is UI pagination only, not a cap on how many nodes can exist.** The colony GUI can assign/cancel resident restock jobs and inspect node stock and reservations.
+
+## Files changed
+
+- `include/galaxy/Simulation.hpp`, `src/Simulation.cpp`, `src/Persistence.cpp`: authoritative custody, reservation, snapshot, ledger and capacity validation.
+- `include/galaxy/NpcConstructionCrews.hpp`, `src/NpcConstructionCrews.cpp`: worker reservations, deterministic supply sources, durable restocking assignments and movement.
+- `src/ColonyStructurePlans.cpp`: permissioned internal supply actions.
+- `src/factory_colony_protocol.hpp`, `live/interactive_relay.py`: host-side REST/RPC validation and visible supply status.
+- `viewer/interactive.html`, `viewer/structures.js`: colony-owned storage-source and crew supply controls.
+- `tests/ECON02B2d8MultiSourceAllocationsTests.cpp`: new test of multi-source competition, restart, capacity, cancellation, salvage and persisted worker cargo.
+- `tests/ECON02B2d6WorldFixture.cpp`, `tests/ECON02B2d6ConstructionCrewHostTests.py`: real localhost restock transfer, hostile token rejection, malformed destination rejection, legacy crew continuation.
+- `scripts/colony_crew_browser_smoke.py`: mocked-browser control behavior (not counted as actual resource validation); additional tests remain in existing source.
+- `CMakeLists.txt`: new native test target and CTest registration.
+
+## Verification completed in local Linux environment
+
+| Check | Verified outcome |
+| --- | --- |
+| Entire native CMake build | **Pass**, completed after incremental rebuild; initial long build was stopped by tool execution limit, not a compiler diagnostic |
+| CTest excluding `live`, `relay`, `_e2e`, `_HTTP` and `_http` | **65 / 65 passed** |
+| Complementary CTest live, relay, E2E and HTTP group | **28 / 28 passed** |
+| Overall CTest count across two disjoint groups | **93 / 93 passed** |
+| JavaScript `node --test tests/*.js` | **93 / 93 passed** |
+| Offline Chromium colony structure UI | **Passed** |
+| Offline Chromium crew/stock/restock UI | **Passed** |
+| New multi-source allocation native test | **Passed** |
+| Existing d7 material hauling and d6 crew native tests | **Passed** |
+| Real localhost HTTP crew test | **Passed**; token validation and actual NPC depot-to-node delivery, original construction and restart |
+| Patch / archive integrity | Verified during package generation with clean `git apply` and manifest hashes |
+
+`tests/*.cjs` are standalone scripts that require executable command-line parameters supplied by their specific CTest targets; blindly invoking `node --test tests/*.cjs` **without** arguments produces a harness error and is not the correct JavaScript suite. The supported JavaScript regression command is `node --test tests/*.js`.
+
+## Engineering boundaries and follow-up work
+
+1. **Not yet 3D NPC navigation:** the physical route is an outpost cell grid. Obstacles and door states influence local paths but there is no planetary navmesh, loading/unloading dock animation, vehicle route, or long-haul cargo ship execution.
+2. **No free cross-site transfer:** these storage nodes belong to the same currently owned constructed outpost. No same-world inter-colony logistics or trade contracts yet.
+3. **Reservations are physical and exclusive** but this is the first deterministic allocator. It is not yet a predictive, multi-factory global planner; reservation expiry, priority preemption and transport congestion require separate policy decisions.
+4. **Manual salvage remains explicit:** unfinished delivered modules can be recovered into a worker's real cargo, but automated cleanup of all orphaned deliveries is not included. No instant refund or mass creation is permitted.
+5. **Host security boundary:** low-level stock transfer Actions are intended for the trusted native simulation and its validated scheduling path. The user-facing HTTP relay offers constrained queue/cancel operations, not arbitrary transfer Actions.
+6. **Windows graphical execution not verified.** Linux native, relay and Chromium tests passed. Do not treat these as evidence that a Windows installer or complete 3D game is ready.
+7. **Next milestone recommendation:** robust allocation policies for prioritized construction queues and source depletion/reassignment, with capacity-aware transport/workforce scheduling and no arbitrary factory-size caps. Keep factory tasks under the colony session and resident job system.
+
+## Reproducibility
+
+Apply the accompanying `.diff` to the exact baseline d7 source snapshot. The generated ZIP includes complete source, new test and this engineering report. Use `cmake -S . -B build -DBUILD_TESTING=ON`, `cmake --build build`, and `ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure`. JavaScript: `node --test tests/*.js`. The original zip baseline and output patch are byte-to-byte source reproducible apart from ZIP container metadata.
